{% doc %}
  One jersey tile. Shared by the homepage grid and the shop page, which use the
  same tile by design.

  The year sits behind the text on the tile's bottom border, drawn in the
  product's own accent colour. Both come from metafields, so a sixth jersey
  needs no template work.

  @param {object} product - The product to render.
  @param {number} [index] - Position in the grid, shown as the small number.
  @param {boolean} [quick_add] - Whether hovering reveals the size row.
  @param {string} [loading] - Image loading hint.

  @example
  {% render 'brand-product-tile', product: product, index: forloop.index, quick_add: true %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign year = product.metafields.jersey.year.value

  comment
    Accent is the dot — the jersey's own colour. The year behind the tile can
    need a different one: Saudi '22's dot is off-white, which would be invisible
    as a tint on white, so its year carries the shirt's green instead.
  endcomment
  assign accent = product.metafields.jersey.accent.value
  assign year_tint = product.metafields.jersey.year_tint.value | default: accent

  comment
    The line under the name is the moment — "Lusail. 2–1." — not the product
    description, which carries the make and belongs on the product page. It has
    its own metafield so the two can say different things. Left empty, the tile
    simply shows name and price.
  endcomment
  assign blurb = product.metafields.jersey.tagline.value | strip_html | strip

  comment
    Only the reveal stagger — the number shown on the tile is the jersey's place
    in the run, not its place in this grid. `render` does not inherit the
    caller's scope, so the grid position has to be handed in.
  endcomment
  assign stagger = index | default: 1 | minus: 1 | times: 90
-%}

<article class="brand-tile" data-reveal="{{ stagger }}">
  {%- if year != blank -%}
    <span class="brand-tile__year" {% if year_tint %}style="color: {{ year_tint }}"{% endif %} aria-hidden="true">
      {{- year -}}
    </span>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="brand-tile__frame">
    {%- if product.featured_media -%}
      {{
        product.featured_media
        | image_url: width: 1200
        | image_tag:
          width: 600,
          widths: '300, 450, 600, 900, 1200',
          sizes: '(min-width: 760px) 33vw, 50vw',
          loading: loading,
          alt: product.featured_media.alt
          | default: product.title
      }}
    {%- else -%}
      {{ 'product-apparel-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'brand-tile__placeholder' }}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if quick_add and product.available -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Each chip is a one-click add for that size. Hidden until hover, and
        never shown on touch, where there is no hover to reveal it.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <brand-quick-add class="brand-tile__sizes" data-product-title="{{ product.title | escape }}">
        {%- for variant in product.variants -%}
          <button
            type="button"
            class="brand-tile__size"
            data-variant-id="{{ variant.id }}"
            aria-label="{{ variant.title }}"
            {% unless variant.available %}
              disabled
            {% endunless %}
          >
            {%- render 'brand-size-label', label: variant.title -%}
          </button>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </brand-quick-add>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Compact is the related-jerseys row at the foot of a product page: the stock
    state moves up beside the number, so the price stands on its own.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <p class="brand-tile__meta{% if compact %} brand-tile__meta--split{% endif %}">
    <span class="brand-tile__number">
      {%- if accent -%}
        <span class="brand-tile__dot" style="background: {{ accent }}"></span>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- render 'brand-run-number', product: product -%}
    </span>

    {%- if compact -%}
      {% render 'brand-stock-state', product: product, compact: true %}
    {%- endif -%}
  </p>

  <h3 class="brand-tile__title">
    <a href="{{ product.url }}">{{ product.title }}</a>
  </h3>

  {%- if blurb != blank -%}
    <p class="brand-tile__blurb">{{ blurb }}</p>
  {%- endif -%}

  <p class="brand-tile__price">
    <span>{{ product.price | money }}</span>
    {%- unless compact -%}
      {% render 'brand-stock-state', product: product, compact: true %}
    {%- endunless -%}
  </p>
</article>

{% stylesheet %}
  /* The grid lives here rather than in a section, because the homepage and the
     shop page lay the same tiles out the same way. */
  .brand-grid {
    display: grid;

    /* Two up until there is room for the full row. */
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    border-bottom: var(--brand-rule);
  }

  .brand-grid .brand-tile:nth-child(2n) {
    border-right: 0;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 1040px) {
    .brand-grid--3 {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }

    .brand-grid--4 {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }

    /* The two-up rule has to be undone first, or every second tile keeps
       losing its divider. */
    .brand-grid .brand-tile:nth-child(2n) {
      border-right: var(--brand-rule);
    }

    .brand-grid--3 .brand-tile:nth-child(3n),
    .brand-grid--4 .brand-tile:nth-child(4n) {
      border-right: 0;
    }
  }

  .brand-tile {
    position: relative;

    /* Keeps the year's negative z-index inside the tile rather than punching
       through to the page background. */
    isolation: isolate;
    overflow: hidden;
    padding-bottom: 22px;
    border-right: var(--brand-rule);
    border-bottom: var(--brand-rule);
  }

  .brand-tile__year {
    position: absolute;
    right: -6px;
    bottom: 0;
    z-index: -1;
    font: var(--brand-type-year);
    letter-spacing: var(--brand-tracking-year);
    opacity: 0.18;
    pointer-events: none;
    user-select: none;
  }

  .brand-tile__frame {
    position: relative;
    aspect-ratio: 3 / 4;
    background: var(--brand-bone);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .brand-tile__frame img,
  .brand-tile__placeholder {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }

  .brand-tile__sizes {
    position: absolute;
    left: 10px;
    right: 10px;
    bottom: 10px;
    display: flex;
    gap: 5px;
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(8px);
    transition:
      opacity var(--brand-transition),
      transform var(--brand-transition);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .brand-tile:hover .brand-tile__sizes,
  .brand-tile:focus-within .brand-tile__sizes {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: none;
    pointer-events: auto;
  }

  .brand-tile__size {
    flex: 1;
    padding-block: 10px;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: var(--brand-radius);
    background: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.95);
    color: var(--brand-navy);
    font: var(--brand-type-label);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background-color var(--brand-transition);
  }

  .brand-tile__size:hover {
    background: var(--brand-white);
  }

  .brand-tile__size[disabled] {
    opacity: 0.4;
    cursor: default;
    text-decoration: line-through;
  }

  .brand-tile__meta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 9px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 16px 18px 0;
    font: var(--brand-type-label);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: rgb(var(--brand-navy-rgb) / 0.5);
  }

  .brand-tile__meta--split {
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .brand-tile__number {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 9px;
  }

  /* The grid draws the closing line for this row, so the tiles do not. */
  .brand-grid--flush {
    border-top: var(--brand-rule);
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  .brand-tile__dot {
    flex: none;
    width: 9px;
    height: 9px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgb(var(--brand-navy-rgb) / 0.25);
  }

  .brand-tile__title {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 9px 18px 0;
    font: var(--brand-type-card-title);
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .brand-tile__title a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .brand-tile__title a:hover {
    color: var(--brand-body-muted);
  }

  .brand-tile__blurb {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 5px 18px 0;
    font: var(--brand-type-body-sm);
    font-size: 0.84375rem;
    color: rgb(var(--brand-navy-rgb) / 0.55);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .brand-tile__price {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;

    /* Two tiles across a phone leaves about 144px here. Price and stock state
       sit side by side when they fit and stack when they do not, rather than
       the second one running off the edge. */
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px 10px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 11px 18px 0;
  }

  .brand-tile__price > span:first-child {
    font: 600 0.875rem / 1 var(--brand-font-display);
  }

  /* No hover to reveal on, so the size row would be unreachable. */
  @media (hover: none) {
    .brand-tile__sizes {
      display: none;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
